    `the Authority has approved the corporation under section 9(1)(a) as an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority approved the corporation under section 9(1)(a) as an approved exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "approved exchange" the corporation is approved exchange` MEANS
    IF `the person is a corporation` AND `the Authority has approved the corporation under section 9(1)(a) as an approved exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a corporation that is approved by the Authority under section 9(1)(a) as an approved exchange"

