§ `s 2(1): rules, listing and quotation`

-- src:1831 | “business rules”, in relation to an approved holding company, an
-- src:1832 | approved exchange, a recognised market operator, a licensed
-- src:1833 | trade repository, a licensed foreign trade repository, an
-- src:1834 | approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house,
-- src:1835 | means the rules, regulations, by‑laws or such similar body of
-- src:1836 | statements, by whatever name called, that govern the
-- src:1837 | activities and conduct of —
-- src:1839 | (a) the approved holding company, approved exchange,
-- src:1840 | recognised market operator, approved clearing house
-- src:1841 | or recognised clearing house and its members, or the
-- src:1842 | licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade
-- src:1843 | repository and its participants; and
-- src:1845 | (b) other persons in relation to it,
-- src:1847 | whether or not those rules, regulations, by‑laws or similar
-- src:1848 | body of statements are made by the approved holding
-- src:1849 | company, approved exchange, recognised market operator,
-- src:1850 | licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository,
-- src:1851 | approved clearing house or recognised clearing house or are
-- src:1852 | contained in its constituent documents; but does not include
-- src:1853 | the listing rules of an approved exchange or a recognised
-- src:1854 | market operator (which is an overseas exchange);
@ref s 2(1) "business rules" (src:1831-1854)
GIVEN
    `the body is an approved holding company, approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an approved holding company, approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house?
    `the statements are rules, regulations, by-laws or a similar body of statements, by whatever name called` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they rules, regulations, by-laws or a similar body of statements, by whatever name called?
    `they govern the activities and conduct of the body and its members, or of the trade repository and its participants` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they govern the activities and conduct of the body and its members (or, for a trade repository, its participants)?
    `they govern the activities and conduct of other persons in relation to the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they govern the activities and conduct of other persons in relation to the body?
    `they are the listing rules of an approved exchange or of a recognised market operator that is an overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they the listing rules of an approved exchange, or of a recognised market operator (which is an overseas exchange)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "business rules" the statements are the business rules of the body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the body is an approved holding company, approved exchange, recognised market operator, licensed trade repository, licensed foreign trade repository, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an approved holding company, an approved exchange, a recognised market operator, a licensed trade repository, a licensed foreign trade repository, an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house"
        IF `they are the listing rules of an approved exchange or of a recognised market operator that is an overseas exchange`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but does not include the listing rules of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator (which is an overseas exchange)"
        IF `the statements are rules, regulations, by-laws or a similar body of statements, by whatever name called` AND `they govern the activities and conduct of the body and its members, or of the trade repository and its participants` AND `they govern the activities and conduct of other persons in relation to the body`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the rules, regulations, by-laws or such similar body of statements, by whatever name called, that govern the activities and conduct of (a) ... and (b) other persons in relation to it"

-- src:2654 | “listing rules”, in relation to a corporation that establishes or
-- src:2655 | operates, or proposes to establish or operate, an organised
-- src:2656 | market of an approved exchange or a recognised market
-- src:2657 | operator, or an overseas exchange that establishes or operates
-- src:2658 | or proposes to establish or operate an organised market of a
-- src:2659 | recognised market operator, means rules governing or
-- src:2660 | relating to —
-- src:2662 | (a) the admission to the official list of the corporation or
-- src:2663 | overseas exchange, of corporations, governments,
-- src:2664 | bodies unincorporate or other persons for the purpose
-- src:2665 | of the quotation on the organised market of the
-- src:2666 | corporation or overseas exchange of securities,
-- src:2667 | securities‑based derivatives contracts or units in a
-- src:2668 | collective investment scheme issued, or made
-- src:2669 | available by such corporations, governments,
-- src:2670 | bodies unincorporate or other persons, or the
-- src:2671 | removal from that official list and for other
-- src:2672 | purposes; or
-- src:2677 | (b) the activities or conduct of corporations,
-- src:2678 | governments, bodies unincorporate and other
-- src:2679 | persons who are admitted to that list,
-- src:2681 | whether those rules are made —
-- src:2683 | (c) by the corporation or overseas exchange, or are
-- src:2684 | contained in any of the constituent documents of the
-- src:2685 | corporation or overseas exchange; or
-- src:2687 | (d) by another person and adopted by the corporation or
-- src:2688 | overseas exchange;
@ref s 2(1) "listing rules" (src:2654-2688)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation that establishes or operates, or proposes to establish or operate, an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator, or an overseas exchange doing so for a recognised market operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation that establishes or operates (or proposes to) an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator, or an overseas exchange that does so for a recognised market operator?
    `the rules govern or relate to the admission to the official list of persons for the quotation of their securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units, or their removal from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rules govern or relate to the admission to the official list of corporations, governments, bodies unincorporate or other persons for the quotation of their securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme, or their removal from it?
    `the rules govern or relate to the activities or conduct of the persons admitted to that list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the rules govern or relate to the activities or conduct of the corporations, governments, bodies unincorporate and other persons admitted to that list?
    `the rules are made by the corporation or overseas exchange, or are contained in its constituent documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules made by the corporation or overseas exchange, or contained in its constituent documents?
    `the rules are made by another person and adopted by the corporation or overseas exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the rules made by another person and adopted by the corporation or overseas exchange?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "listing rules" the rules are the listing rules of the corporation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the body is a corporation that establishes or operates, or proposes to establish or operate, an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator, or an overseas exchange doing so for a recognised market operator`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to a corporation that establishes or operates ... an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator, or an overseas exchange ..."
        IF (`the rules govern or relate to the admission to the official list of persons for the quotation of their securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units, or their removal from it` OR `the rules govern or relate to the activities or conduct of the persons admitted to that list`) AND (`the rules are made by the corporation or overseas exchange, or are contained in its constituent documents` OR `the rules are made by another person and adopted by the corporation or overseas exchange`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means rules governing or relating to (a) the admission to the official list ... ; or (b) the activities or conduct of ... persons who are admitted to that list, whether those rules are made (c) by the corporation or overseas exchange ...; or (d) by another person and adopted by the corporation or overseas exchange"

-- src:2716 | “overseas exchange” means a person operating an organised
-- src:2717 | market outside Singapore that is regulated by a financial
-- src:2718 | services regulatory authority of a country or territory other
-- src:2719 | than Singapore;
@ref s 2(1) "overseas exchange" (src:2716-2719)
GIVEN
    `the person operates an organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person operate an organised market?
    `the organised market is outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organised market outside Singapore?
    `the organised market is regulated by a financial services regulatory authority of a country or territory other than Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the organised market regulated by a financial services regulatory authority of a country or territory other than Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "overseas exchange" the person is an overseas exchange` MEANS
    IF `the person operates an organised market` AND `the organised market is outside Singapore` AND `the organised market is regulated by a financial services regulatory authority of a country or territory other than Singapore`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person operating an organised market outside Singapore that is regulated by a financial services regulatory authority of a country or territory other than Singapore"

-- src:2865 | “quote” means to display or provide, on an organised market of
-- src:2866 | an approved exchange or a recognised market operator,
-- src:2867 | information concerning the particular prices or particular
-- src:2868 | consideration at which offers or invitations to sell, purchase
-- src:2869 | or exchange securities, securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:2874 | or units in a collective investment scheme are made on that
-- src:2875 | organised market, being offers or invitations that are intended
-- src:2876 | or may reasonably be expected, to result, directly or
-- src:2877 | indirectly, in the making or acceptance of offers to sell,
-- src:2878 | purchase or exchange securities, securities‑based derivatives
-- src:2879 | contracts or units in a collective investment scheme;
@ref s 2(1) "quote" (src:2865-2879)
GIVEN
    `the information is displayed or provided on an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information displayed or provided on an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator?
    `the information concerns the particular prices or particular consideration at which offers or invitations to sell, purchase or exchange are made on that organised market` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information concern the particular prices or particular consideration at which offers or invitations to sell, purchase or exchange are made on that organised market?
    `the offers or invitations are of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offers or invitations to sell, purchase or exchange securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme?
    `the offers or invitations are intended, or may reasonably be expected, to result directly or indirectly in the making or acceptance of offers to sell, purchase or exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the offers or invitations intended, or may they reasonably be expected, to result directly or indirectly in the making or acceptance of offers to sell, purchase or exchange those products?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "quote" the display or provision of information is to quote` MEANS
    IF `the information is displayed or provided on an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator` AND `the information concerns the particular prices or particular consideration at which offers or invitations to sell, purchase or exchange are made on that organised market` AND `the offers or invitations are of securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme` AND `the offers or invitations are intended, or may reasonably be expected, to result directly or indirectly in the making or acceptance of offers to sell, purchase or exchange`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means to display or provide, on an organised market of an approved exchange or a recognised market operator, information concerning the particular prices or particular consideration at which offers or invitations to sell, purchase or exchange securities, securities-based derivatives contracts or units in a collective investment scheme are made on that organised market, being offers or invitations that are intended or may reasonably be expected, to result, directly or indirectly, in the making or acceptance of offers"

-- src:2695 | “member”, in relation to an approved exchange, a recognised
-- src:2696 | market operator, an approved clearing house or a recognised
-- src:2697 | clearing house, means a person who holds membership of
-- src:2698 | any class or description in the approved exchange, recognised
-- src:2699 | market operator, approved clearing house or recognised
-- src:2700 | clearing house, whether or not the person holds any share in
-- src:2701 | the share capital of the approved exchange, recognised
-- src:2702 | market operator, approved clearing house or recognised
-- src:2703 | clearing house, as the case may be;
@ref s 2(1) "member" (src:2695-2703)
GIVEN
    `the body is an approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house?
    `the person holds membership of any class or description in the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person hold membership of any class or description in the body (whether or not the person holds any share in its share capital)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "member" the person is a member of the body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the body is an approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to an approved exchange, a recognised market operator, an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house"
        IF `the person holds membership of any class or description in the body`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a person who holds membership of any class or description in the approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house, whether or not the person holds any share in the share capital"

§ `s 2(1): users, transaction information and records`

-- s 2(1) "user": whose user, by the kind of body.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "user" in relation to` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "user" an approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house`
    `s 2(1) "user" a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository`

-- src:3421 | “user” means —
-- src:3423 | (a) in relation to an approved exchange, a recognised
-- src:3424 | market operator, an approved clearing house or a
-- src:3425 | recognised clearing house, a person who is —
-- src:3427 | (i) a member of the approved exchange,
-- src:3428 | recognised market operator, approved
-- src:3429 | clearing house or recognised clearing house,
-- src:3430 | as the case may be; or
-- src:3432 | (ii) a customer of a member of the approved
-- src:3433 | exchange, recognised market operator,
-- src:3434 | approved clearing house or recognised
-- src:3435 | clearing house, as the case may be; or
-- src:3437 | (b) in relation to a licensed trade repository or a licensed
-- src:3438 | foreign trade repository, a person who is —
-- src:3443 | (i) a participant of the licensed trade repository or
-- src:3444 | licensed foreign trade repository; or
-- src:3446 | (ii) a client of a participant of the licensed trade
-- src:3447 | repository or licensed foreign trade repository;
@ref s 2(1) "user" (src:3421-3447)
GIVEN
    `the kind of body` IS A `s 2(1) "user" in relation to` @desc Is the body an approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house; or a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository?
    `the person is a member of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a member of the body?
    `the person is a customer of a member of the body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a customer of a member of the body?
    `the person is a participant of the trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a participant of the trade repository?
    `the person is a client of a participant of the trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a client of a participant of the trade repository?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "user" the person is a user` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of body`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "user" an approved exchange, recognised market operator, approved clearing house or recognised clearing house`
        THEN IF `the person is a member of the body` OR `the person is a customer of a member of the body`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) in relation to an approved exchange, a recognised market operator, an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house, a person who is (i) a member ...; or (ii) a customer of a member"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "user" a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository`
        THEN IF `the person is a participant of the trade repository` OR `the person is a client of a participant of the trade repository`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in relation to a licensed trade repository or a licensed foreign trade repository, a person who is (i) a participant ...; or (ii) a client of a participant"

-- src:3289 | “transaction information” means information relating to —
-- src:3291 | (a) offers or invitations to enter into, purchase, sell, or
-- src:3292 | exchange capital markets products;
-- src:3297 | (b) executed transactions in capital markets products;
-- src:3299 | (c) transactions cleared or settled by an approved
-- src:3300 | clearing house or a recognised clearing house; or
-- src:3302 | (d) transactions reported to a licensed trade repository or
-- src:3303 | licensed foreign trade repository;
@ref s 2(1) "transaction information" (src:3289-3303)
GIVEN
    `the information relates to offers or invitations to enter into, purchase, sell or exchange capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to offers or invitations to enter into, purchase, sell or exchange capital markets products?
    `the information relates to executed transactions in capital markets products` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to executed transactions in capital markets products?
    `the information relates to transactions cleared or settled by an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to transactions cleared or settled by an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house?
    `the information relates to transactions reported to a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the information relate to transactions reported to a licensed trade repository or a licensed foreign trade repository?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "transaction information" the information is transaction information` MEANS
    IF `the information relates to offers or invitations to enter into, purchase, sell or exchange capital markets products` OR `the information relates to executed transactions in capital markets products` OR `the information relates to transactions cleared or settled by an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house` OR `the information relates to transactions reported to a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means information relating to (a) offers or invitations to enter into, purchase, sell, or exchange capital markets products; (b) executed transactions in capital markets products; (c) transactions cleared or settled by an approved clearing house or a recognised clearing house; or (d) transactions reported to a licensed trade repository or licensed foreign trade repository"

-- src:3449 | “user information” means transaction information that is
-- src:3450 | referable to —
-- src:3452 | (a) a named user; or
-- src:3454 | (b) a group of users, from which the name of a user can
-- src:3455 | be directly inferred;
@ref s 2(1) "user information" (src:3449-3455)
GIVEN
    `the information is transaction information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information transaction information as section 2(1) defines it?
    `the information is referable to a named user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information referable to a named user?
    `the information is referable to a group of users from which the name of a user can be directly inferred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information referable to a group of users from which the name of a user can be directly inferred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "user information" the information is user information` MEANS
    IF `the information is transaction information` AND (`the information is referable to a named user` OR `the information is referable to a group of users from which the name of a user can be directly inferred`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means transaction information that is referable to (a) a named user; or (b) a group of users, from which the name of a user can be directly inferred"

-- src:1825 | “book” includes any record, register, document or other record
-- src:1826 | of information, and any account or accounting record,
-- src:1827 | however compiled, recorded or stored, whether in written
-- src:1828 | or printed form or on microfilm or in any other electronic
-- src:1829 | form or otherwise;
@ref s 2(1) "book" (src:1825-1829)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a record, register, document or other record of information, however compiled, recorded or stored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a record, register, document or other record of information, however compiled, recorded or stored (in written or printed form, on microfilm, in electronic form or otherwise)?
    `the thing is an account or accounting record, however compiled, recorded or stored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing an account or accounting record, however compiled, recorded or stored?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "book" the thing is a book` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a record, register, document or other record of information, however compiled, recorded or stored` OR `the thing is an account or accounting record, however compiled, recorded or stored`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "book includes any record, register, document or other record of information, and any account or accounting record" lists without closing the list

-- src:2910 | “record” means information that is inscribed, stored or
-- src:2911 | otherwise fixed on a tangible medium or that is stored in
-- src:2912 | an electronic or other medium and is retrievable in
-- src:2913 | perceivable form;
@ref s 2(1) "record" (src:2910-2913)
GIVEN
    `the information is inscribed, stored or otherwise fixed on a tangible medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information inscribed, stored or otherwise fixed on a tangible medium?
    `the information is stored in an electronic or other medium` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information stored in an electronic or other medium?
    `the information is retrievable in perceivable form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information retrievable in perceivable form?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "record" the information is a record` MEANS
    IF `the information is inscribed, stored or otherwise fixed on a tangible medium` OR (`the information is stored in an electronic or other medium` AND `the information is retrievable in perceivable form`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means information that is inscribed, stored or otherwise fixed on a tangible medium or that is stored in an electronic or other medium and is retrievable in perceivable form"

-- src:2348 | “defalcation” means misapplication, including
-- src:2349 | misappropriation, of any property;
@ref s 2(1) "defalcation" (src:2348-2349)
GIVEN
    `the act is a misapplication of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a misapplication of property?
    `the act is a misappropriation of property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the act a misappropriation of property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "defalcation" the act is a defalcation` MEANS
    IF `the act is a misapplication of property` OR `the act is a misappropriation of property`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means misapplication, including misappropriation, of any property"

§ `s 2(1): prohibition orders and the written laws the Act lists`

