@ref s 2(1) "related Acts prohibition order" (src:2940-2970)
GIVEN
    `the order is a prohibition order made under section 68(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 as in force immediately before the commencement of section 200(1)(b) and (2) to (7) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order a prohibition order made under section 68(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 as in force immediately before the commencement of section 200(1)(b) and (2) to (7) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022?
    `the order is such a prohibition order, as continued by section 217(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order such a prohibition order as continued by section 217(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022?
    `the order is an order made under section 74(1) of the Insurance Act 1966 as in force immediately before the commencement of section 204(1) to (4) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order an order made under section 74(1) of the Insurance Act 1966 as in force immediately before the commencement of section 204(1) to (4) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022?
    `the order is such an order under the Insurance Act 1966, as continued by section 218(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order such an order under the Insurance Act 1966 as continued by section 218(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "related Acts prohibition order" the order is a related Acts prohibition order` MEANS
    IF `the order is a prohibition order made under section 68(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 as in force immediately before the commencement of section 200(1)(b) and (2) to (7) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` OR `the order is such a prohibition order, as continued by section 217(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` OR `the order is an order made under section 74(1) of the Insurance Act 1966 as in force immediately before the commencement of section 204(1) to (4) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` OR `the order is such an order under the Insurance Act 1966, as continued by section 218(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) a prohibition order made under section 68(1) of the Financial Advisers Act 2001 ...; (b) ... and as continued by section 217(2) ...; (c) an order made under section 74(1) of the Insurance Act 1966 ...; or (d) ... and as continued by section 218(2) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022"

