-- s 2(1) "prescribed written law": the Acts the definition names, as a list a person can pick from, and which paragraph is read.
DECLARE `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the written law` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" this Act`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Banking Act 1970`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Credit Bureau Act 2016`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes Act 2011`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Finance Companies Act 1967`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Advisers Act 2001`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Holding Companies Act 2013`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Insurance Act 1966`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Payment Services Act 2019`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Trust Companies Act 2005`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" some other written law`

DECLARE `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" for the purpose of Division 3 of Part 9`
    `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" for the purpose of any other provision`

-- src:2756 | “prescribed written law” means —
-- src:2758 | (a) for the purpose of Division 3 of Part 9 — this Act or
-- src:2759 | any of the following Acts, and any subsidiary
-- src:2760 | legislation made under this Act or those Acts:
-- src:2762 | (i) Banking Act 1970;
-- src:2764 | (ii) Credit Bureau Act 2016;
-- src:2766 | (iii) Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners’
-- src:2767 | Protection Schemes Act 2011;
-- src:2772 | (iv) Finance Companies Act 1967;
-- src:2774 | (v) Financial Advisers Act 2001;
-- src:2776 | (vi) Financial Holding Companies Act 2013;
-- src:2778 | (vii) Financial Services and Markets Act 2022;
-- src:2780 | (viii) Insurance Act 1966;
-- src:2782 | (ix) Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970;
-- src:2784 | (x) Payment Services Act 2019;
-- src:2786 | (xi) Trust Companies Act 2005;
-- src:2788 | (xii) such other written law as the Authority may
-- src:2789 | prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:2790 | section 341; and
-- src:2792 | (b) for the purpose of any other provision — this Act or
-- src:2793 | any of the following Acts, and any subsidiary
-- src:2794 | legislation made thereunder:
-- src:2796 | (i) Banking Act 1970;
-- src:2798 | (ii) Finance Companies Act 1967;
-- src:2800 | (iii) Financial Advisers Act 2001;
-- src:2802 | (iv) Financial Services and Markets Act 2022;
-- src:2804 | (v) Insurance Act 1966;
-- src:2806 | (vi) Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970;
-- src:2808 | (vii) Payment Services Act 2019;
-- src:2810 | (viii) such other written law as the Authority may
-- src:2811 | prescribe by regulations made under
-- src:2812 | section 341;
@ref s 2(1) "prescribed written law" (src:2756-2812)
GIVEN
    `the purpose the term is read for` IS A `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" purpose` @desc Is "prescribed written law" being read for Division 3 of Part 9, or for any other provision?
    `the written law` IS A `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the written law` @desc Which written law is it: this Act, the Banking Act 1970, the Credit Bureau Act 2016, the Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes Act 2011, the Finance Companies Act 1967, the Financial Advisers Act 2001, the Financial Holding Companies Act 2013, the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022, the Insurance Act 1966, the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970, the Payment Services Act 2019, the Trust Companies Act 2005, or some other written law? (For subsidiary legislation, give the Act it is made under.)
    `the Authority has prescribed the written law by regulations under section 341` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed the written law, by regulations made under section 341, for this purpose?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the written law is a prescribed written law` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the purpose the term is read for`
    WHEN `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" for the purpose of Division 3 of Part 9`
        THEN IF `the Authority has prescribed the written law by regulations under section 341`
                OR (`the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" this Act` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Banking Act 1970` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Credit Bureau Act 2016` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes Act 2011` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Finance Companies Act 1967` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Holding Companies Act 2013` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Insurance Act 1966` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Payment Services Act 2019` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Trust Companies Act 2005`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) for the purpose of Division 3 of Part 9 this Act or any of the following Acts, and any subsidiary legislation made under this Act or those Acts: (i) Banking Act 1970; (ii) Credit Bureau Act 2016; (iii) Deposit Insurance and Policy Owners' Protection Schemes Act 2011; (iv) Finance Companies Act 1967; (v) Financial Advisers Act 2001; (vi) Financial Holding Companies Act 2013; (vii) Financial Services and Markets Act 2022; (viii) Insurance Act 1966; (ix) Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970; (x) Payment Services Act 2019; (xi) Trust Companies Act 2005; (xii) such other written law as the Authority may prescribe"
    WHEN `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" for the purpose of any other provision`
        THEN IF `the Authority has prescribed the written law by regulations under section 341`
                OR (`the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" this Act` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Banking Act 1970` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Finance Companies Act 1967` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Advisers Act 2001` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Financial Services and Markets Act 2022` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Insurance Act 1966` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970` OR `the written law` EQUALS `s 2(1) "prescribed written law" the Payment Services Act 2019`)
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) for the purpose of any other provision this Act or any of the following Acts, and any subsidiary legislation made thereunder: (i) Banking Act 1970; (ii) Finance Companies Act 1967; (iii) Financial Advisers Act 2001; (iv) Financial Services and Markets Act 2022; (v) Insurance Act 1966; (vi) Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970; (vii) Payment Services Act 2019; (viii) such other written law as the Authority may prescribe"

§ `s 2(1): take-over offer`

-- src:3186 | “take‑over offer” means —
-- src:3188 | (a) an offer for the acquisition by or on behalf of a person
-- src:3189 | of —
-- src:3191 | (i) in the case of a public company, or of a
-- src:3192 | corporation all or any of the shares of which are
-- src:3193 | listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:3194 | exchange —
-- src:3196 | (A) some or all of the shares, or some or all of
-- src:3197 | the shares of a particular class, in the
-- src:3198 | company or corporation made to all
-- src:3199 | members of the company or
-- src:3200 | corporation, or where the person already
-- src:3201 | holds shares in the company or
-- src:3206 | corporation, made to all other members
-- src:3207 | of the company or corporation; or
-- src:3209 | (B) all of the remaining shares in the
-- src:3210 | company or corporation made to all
-- src:3211 | other members of the company or
-- src:3212 | corporation as a result of the person
-- src:3213 | acquiring or consolidating effective
-- src:3214 | control of that company or corporation
-- src:3215 | within the meaning of the Take‑over
-- src:3216 | Code;
-- src:3218 | (ii) in the case of a registered business trust, or of a
-- src:3219 | business trust all or any of the units of which
-- src:3220 | are listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:3221 | exchange —
-- src:3223 | (A) some or all of the units, or some or all of
-- src:3224 | the units of a particular class, in the
-- src:3225 | business trust made to all unitholders of
-- src:3226 | the business trust, or where the person
-- src:3227 | already holds units in the business trust,
-- src:3228 | made to all other unitholders of the
-- src:3229 | business trust; or
-- src:3231 | (B) all of the remaining units in the business
-- src:3232 | trust made to all other unitholders of the
-- src:3233 | business trust as a result of the person
-- src:3234 | acquiring or consolidating effective
-- src:3235 | control of that business trust within the
-- src:3236 | meaning of the Take‑over Code; or
-- src:3238 | (iii) in the case of a collective investment scheme
-- src:3239 | constituted as a unit trust and authorised under
-- src:3240 | section 286, that invests primarily in real estate
-- src:3241 | and real estate‑related assets specified by the
-- src:3242 | Authority in the Code on Collective Investment
-- src:3243 | Schemes, and all or any of the units in which
-- src:3244 | are listed for quotation on an approved
-- src:3245 | exchange —
-- src:3250 | (A) some or all of the units, or some or all of
-- src:3251 | the units of a particular class, in the
-- src:3252 | scheme made to all unitholders of the
-- src:3253 | scheme, or where the person already
-- src:3254 | holds units in the scheme, made to all
-- src:3255 | other unitholders of the scheme; or
-- src:3257 | (B) all of the remaining units in the scheme
-- src:3258 | made to all other unitholders of the
-- src:3259 | scheme as a result of the person
-- src:3260 | acquiring or consolidating effective
-- src:3261 | control of that scheme within the
-- src:3262 | meaning of the Take‑over Code; or
-- src:3264 | (b) a proposed compromise or arrangement which —
-- src:3266 | (i) in the case of a public company, is referred to in
-- src:3267 | section 210 of the Companies Act 1967; or
-- src:3269 | (ii) in the case of a corporation all or any of the
-- src:3270 | shares of which are listed for quotation on an
-- src:3271 | approved exchange, complies with the laws,
-- src:3272 | codes and other requirements (whether or not
-- src:3273 | having the force of law) relating to take‑overs,
-- src:3274 | compromises and arrangements of the country
-- src:3275 | or territory in which that corporation was
-- src:3276 | incorporated,
-- src:3278 | (b) and which, if executed, would result in a change in
-- src:3279 | effective control of the public company or
-- src:3280 | corporation within the meaning of the Take‑over
-- src:3281 | Code;
@ref s 2(1) "take-over offer" (src:3186-3281)
GIVEN
    `the target is a public company, or a corporation all or any of whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the target a public company, or a corporation all or any of whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the target is a registered business trust, or a business trust all or any of whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the target a registered business trust, or a business trust all or any of whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the target is a collective investment scheme constituted as a unit trust, authorised under section 286, that invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes, and all or any of its units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the target a collective investment scheme constituted as a unit trust and authorised under section 286, investing primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified by the Authority in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes, with all or any of its units listed for quotation on an approved exchange?
    `the offer is for some or all of the shares or units, or of a particular class, made to all members or unitholders, or where the offeror already holds some, to all the others` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer for the acquisition of some or all of the shares or units (or some or all of a particular class), made to all the members or unitholders, or (where the offeror already holds some) to all the other members or unitholders?
    `the offer is for all of the remaining shares or units, made to all the other members or unitholders as a result of the offeror acquiring or consolidating effective control within the meaning of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer for all of the remaining shares or units, made to all the other members or unitholders as a result of the offeror acquiring or consolidating effective control within the meaning of the Take-over Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "take-over offer" (a) the offer is a take-over offer by acquisition` MEANS
    IF (`the target is a public company, or a corporation all or any of whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` OR `the target is a registered business trust, or a business trust all or any of whose units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange` OR `the target is a collective investment scheme constituted as a unit trust, authorised under section 286, that invests primarily in real estate and real estate-related assets specified in the Code on Collective Investment Schemes, and all or any of its units are listed for quotation on an approved exchange`) AND (`the offer is for some or all of the shares or units, or of a particular class, made to all members or unitholders, or where the offeror already holds some, to all the others` OR `the offer is for all of the remaining shares or units, made to all the other members or unitholders as a result of the offeror acquiring or consolidating effective control within the meaning of the Take-over Code`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means (a) an offer for the acquisition by or on behalf of a person of (i) in the case of a public company, or of a corporation all or any of the shares of which are listed ..., (A) some or all of the shares ... made to all members ...; or (B) all of the remaining shares ...; (ii) in the case of a registered business trust ...; or (iii) in the case of a collective investment scheme constituted as a unit trust ..."

GIVEN
    `the proposal is a compromise or arrangement of a public company referred to in section 210 of the Companies Act 1967` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal a compromise or arrangement, of a public company, referred to in section 210 of the Companies Act 1967?
    `the proposal is a compromise or arrangement of a corporation all or any of whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, that complies with the take-over, compromise and arrangement laws and codes of its country of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal a compromise or arrangement of a corporation all or any of whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, that complies with the laws, codes and other requirements relating to take-overs, compromises and arrangements of the country or territory in which the corporation was incorporated?
    `if executed it would result in a change in effective control of the public company or corporation within the meaning of the Take-over Code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If executed, would it result in a change in effective control of the public company or corporation within the meaning of the Take-over Code?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "take-over offer" (b) the proposal is a take-over offer by compromise or arrangement` MEANS
    IF (`the proposal is a compromise or arrangement of a public company referred to in section 210 of the Companies Act 1967` OR `the proposal is a compromise or arrangement of a corporation all or any of whose shares are listed for quotation on an approved exchange, that complies with the take-over, compromise and arrangement laws and codes of its country of incorporation`) AND `if executed it would result in a change in effective control of the public company or corporation within the meaning of the Take-over Code`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a proposed compromise or arrangement which (i) in the case of a public company, is referred to in section 210 of the Companies Act 1967; or (ii) in the case of a corporation all or any of the shares of which are listed ..., complies with the laws, codes and other requirements ... and which, if executed, would result in a change in effective control of the public company or corporation within the meaning of the Take-over Code"

GIVEN
    `the proposal is an offer within paragraph (a) of the definition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal an offer for acquisition within paragraph (a) of the definition?
    `the proposal is a compromise or arrangement within paragraph (b) of the definition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proposal a compromise or arrangement within paragraph (b) of the definition?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) "take-over offer" the proposal is a take-over offer` MEANS
    IF `the proposal is an offer within paragraph (a) of the definition` OR `the proposal is a compromise or arrangement within paragraph (b) of the definition`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): ""take-over offer" means (a) ...; or (b) ..."
